title: "Bounds on recursive self-improvement"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nicole
    family-names: Welch
    affiliation: "Hestia's Creations"
  - given-names: Timothy
    family-names: Miller Allen
    affiliation: "Hestia's Creations"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hestia-s-Creations/rsi-bounds"
date-released: 2026-10-20
version: 0.2.0
license: "GPL-3.0-or-later"
abstract: >-
  Information-theoretic bounds on recursive self-improvement (knowledge grows by at most the
  input bits and never past memory; sustained learning forces forgetting at the same rate; two
  minds know no more than their combined inputs), a conditional growth law for compute-only
  skill, an undecidability result for general prediction, numerical checks, Lean 4 proofs of
  the counting forms, and a pre-registered sensor experiment protocol.
